msgid ""
"Maximum cloud cover of a whole scene in percent. Scenes that are cloudier"
" are not used at all. This scene filter complements ``scl_classes``, "
"which removes single pixels."
msgstr ""
"Maximale Wolkenbedeckung einer ganzen Szene in Prozent. Wolkigere Szenen "
"werden gar nicht verwendet. Dieser Szenenfilter ergänzt ``scl_classes``, "
"das einzelne Pixel entfernt."

#: cdec.eo.evi.download_enhanced_vegetation_index:26
#: cdec.eo.ndmi.download_normalized_difference_moisture_index:29
#: cdec.eo.ndvi.download_normalized_difference_vegetation_index:23 of
msgid ""
"Scene Classification Layer (SCL) classes to **keep**, as a tuple of class"
" IDs. The default ``SCL_LAND`` = ``(4, 5)`` keeps vegetation and non-"
"vegetated land and drops water, clouds, cirrus, shadows, snow/ice, "
"unclassified and defective pixels. Use ``SCL_LAND_AND_WATER`` = ``(4, 5, "
"6)`` to also keep water, or ``None`` to switch SCL masking off. Run "
"``cdec.show_scl_classes()`` to see what each class means. Pixels without "
"any retained observation remain no data."
msgstr ""
"Klassen der Scene Classification Layer (SCL), die **behalten** werden, "
"als Tupel von Klassen-IDs. Der Standard ``SCL_LAND`` = ``(4, 5)`` behält "
"Vegetation und nicht bewachsenes Land und verwirft Wasser, Wolken, "
"Zirren, Schatten, Schnee/Eis, nicht klassifizierte und defekte Pixel. "
"Verwende ``SCL_LAND_AND_WATER`` = ``(4, 5, 6)``, um auch Wasser zu "
"behalten, oder ``None``, um die SCL-Maskierung auszuschalten. Führe "
"``cdec.show_scl_classes()`` aus, um zu sehen, was jede Klasse bedeutet. "
"Pixel ohne eine einzige behaltene Beobachtung bleiben ohne Daten."

